---
// A0 poster for "Fixed RAG Compression Collapses Measured Reader Scaling"
// (arXiv:2606.21807). Every number comes from the frozen official-score
// analysis in the research repo (memory-eligibility-feasibility,
// journal/results/official-score-analysis/summary.json) via the current
// manuscript; keep in sync with it. All figures are drawn poster-native here
// (see poster.md principle 6). Color code: HotpotQA/RECOMP = rc blue,
// MuSiQue/shared summary = rc amber, raw evidence = neutral ink.
import PosterShell from '../../components/poster/PosterShell.astro';
import PosterCell from '../../components/poster/PosterCell.astro';
import TitleBand from '../../components/poster/TitleBand.astro';

const ink = 'rgb(var(--color-ink-dark))';
const muted = 'rgb(var(--color-ink-muted))';
const hpC = 'rgb(var(--color-rc-hp))';
const mqC = 'rgb(var(--color-rc-mq))';
const paper = 'rgb(var(--color-paper-surface))';

// ── Figure ③: reader scaling under one fixed artifact (paper Figure 2) ──
// Per-reader means from the frozen row_scores matrix; raw ascending.
// Endpoints (first/last) are the raw-selected pair used for retention.
const hpPts = [
  [0.126, 0.364], [0.144, 0.358], [0.182, 0.388], [0.188, 0.338],
  [0.234, 0.378], [0.306, 0.454], [0.342, 0.404], [0.344, 0.392],
  [0.344, 0.412], [0.346, 0.412], [0.358, 0.38], [0.366, 0.43],
  [0.37, 0.39], [0.384, 0.456], [0.384, 0.366], [0.43, 0.418],
  [0.432, 0.434], [0.436, 0.412], [0.438, 0.442], [0.444, 0.442],
];
const mqPts = [
  [0.045, 0.426], [0.053, 0.43], [0.065, 0.414], [0.08, 0.364],
  [0.085, 0.395], [0.088, 0.419], [0.138, 0.437], [0.148, 0.43],
  [0.149, 0.426], [0.166, 0.438], [0.168, 0.454], [0.183, 0.436],
  [0.217, 0.436], [0.221, 0.437], [0.232, 0.428],
];
const scalePanels = [
  {
    title: 'HOTPOTQA, FIXED RECOMP, EM',
    pts: hpPts,
    color: hpC,
    readers: '20 readers',
    note: 'retains 24.5% of a 31.8pp contrast',
  },
  {
    title: 'MUSIQUE, SHARED SUMMARY, F1',
    pts: mqPts,
    color: mqC,
    readers: '15 readers',
    note: 'retains 0.8% of an 18.7pp contrast',
  },
];
// Scatter geometry per panel: plot 520×300, both axes 0–50%.
const scX = (p, v) => p * 740 + 120 + (v / 0.5) * 520;
const scY = (v) => 330 - (v / 0.5) * 300;
const scTicks = [0, 0.25, 0.5];

// ── Figure ④: excess ranking flips vs the raw replay floor (paper Fig. 3) ──
const flipRows = [
  { label: 'HotpotQA, EM', c: 16.7, lo: 8.7, hi: 24.4, color: hpC },
  { label: 'HotpotQA, F1', c: 16.7, lo: 8.5, hi: 24.1, color: hpC },
  { label: 'MuSiQue, EM', c: 32.7, lo: 18.6, hi: 45.8, color: mqC },
  { label: 'MuSiQue, F1', c: 21.2, lo: 6.5, hi: 37.7, color: mqC },
];
// Flip geometry: viewBox 1440×470, plot x ∈ [430, 1290] for −5…+50 pts.
const flX = (v) => 430 + ((v + 5) / 55) * 860;
const flTicks = [0, 10, 20, 30, 40, 50];

// ── Figure ⑤: rescue and damage transitions (paper Table 3) ──
const transRows = [
  { label: 'HotpotQA', rescue: 19.1, damage: 35.7, color: hpC },
  { label: 'MuSiQue', rescue: 22.9, damage: 33.8, color: mqC },
];

// ── Figure ⑥: endpoint retention by HotpotQA policy (EM) ──
const policyRows = [
  { label: 'EXIT', ret: 0.836 },
  { label: 'RECOMP extractive', ret: 0.245 },
  { label: 'LLM summary', ret: 0.181 },
  { label: 'RECOMP abstractive', ret: 0.138 },
];
---

<PosterShell
  author="Sugam Panthi"
  title="Poster: Fixed RAG Compression"
  description="A0 research poster: fixed RAG compression collapses measured reader scaling (arXiv:2606.21807)."
  slug="rag-compression"
>
  <TitleBand
    kicker="arXiv:2606.21807, cs.CL. 176,864-row reader-by-compression matrix released"
    title="Fixed RAG Compression Collapses Measured Reader Scaling"
    authors="Sugam Panthi and Rabab Abdelfattah"
    affiliation="Fixed-Artifact Reader Replay: byte-identical compressed evidence replayed across 8 to 20 reader panels"
    qrSrc="/poster/rag-compression-qr.svg"
    qrLabel="Scan for paper"
  />

  <PosterCell span={5} marker="1" kicker="The problem" title="Fixed compression shrinks the measured gap between readers">
    <div class="poster-body">
      <p>
        Compression is evaluated as a deployment layer: does a shorter context preserve accuracy?
        The same layer is then reused while <strong>readers are compared</strong>. These roles
        conflict. A compressor can raise several pipeline scores while
        <span class="rc-hp">absorbing the reader upgrade</span> the evaluation was built to measure.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="poster-figure span-collapse">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 900 250" role="img" aria-label="Two dumbbells: the raw endpoint readers span 12.6 to 44.4 EM; under one fixed RECOMP artifact the same pair spans 36.4 to 44.2.">
        <text x="10" y="30" font-size="20" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="2" fill={ink}>RAW EVIDENCE</text>
        <line x1={10 + (0.126 / 0.5) * 800} y1="62" x2={10 + (0.444 / 0.5) * 800} y2="62" stroke={ink} stroke-width="5" opacity="0.45" />
        <circle cx={10 + (0.126 / 0.5) * 800} cy="62" r="12" fill={paper} stroke={ink} stroke-width="3" />
        <circle cx={10 + (0.444 / 0.5) * 800} cy="62" r="12" fill={ink} />
        <text x={10 + (0.126 / 0.5) * 800} y="102" text-anchor="middle" font-size="21" fill={muted}>12.6</text>
        <text x={10 + (0.444 / 0.5) * 800} y="102" text-anchor="middle" font-size="21" fill={muted}>44.4</text>
        <text x="866" y="69" font-size="23" font-weight="600" fill={ink} text-anchor="end">31.8pp</text>

        <text x="10" y="152" font-size="20" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="2" fill={hpC}>SAME PAIR, FIXED RECOMP</text>
        <line x1={10 + (0.364 / 0.5) * 800} y1="184" x2={10 + (0.442 / 0.5) * 800} y2="184" stroke={hpC} stroke-width="5" opacity="0.55" />
        <circle cx={10 + (0.364 / 0.5) * 800} cy="184" r="12" fill={paper} stroke={hpC} stroke-width="3" />
        <circle cx={10 + (0.442 / 0.5) * 800} cy="184" r="12" fill={hpC} />
        <text x={10 + (0.364 / 0.5) * 800} y="224" text-anchor="middle" font-size="21" fill={muted}>36.4</text>
        <text x={10 + (0.442 / 0.5) * 800} y="224" text-anchor="middle" font-size="21" fill={muted}>44.2</text>
        <text x="866" y="191" font-size="23" font-weight="600" fill={hpC} text-anchor="end">7.8pp</text>
      </svg>
    </figure>
    <p class="big-stat">
      <span class="stat-number">7.8pp</span>
      is all that remains of a 31.8pp raw reader contrast after one useful in-domain RECOMP
      artifact. Same 500 HotpotQA rows, same candidate pools, same endpoint pair.
    </p>
  </PosterCell>

  <PosterCell span={7} marker="2" kicker="Method" title="Fixed-Artifact Reader Replay: change only the evidence policy">
    <figure class="poster-figure">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 520" role="img" aria-label="Flow diagram: frozen candidate pools branch into raw evidence and one hashed compressed artifact per row; both are replayed across 8 to 20 readers, yielding upgrade retention and excess ranking flips.">
        <defs>
          <marker id="rc-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill={muted} />
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <rect x="360" y="16" width="720" height="76" fill={paper} stroke={ink} stroke-width="2.5" />
        <text x="720" y="49" font-size="25" font-weight="600" fill={ink} text-anchor="middle">saved candidate pools per row</text>
        <text x="720" y="78" font-size="21" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">rows, retrieval, prompts, and scorer fixed before replay</text>
        <line x1="540" y1="92" x2="380" y2="148" stroke={muted} stroke-width="3.5" marker-end="url(#rc-arrow)" />
        <line x1="900" y1="92" x2="1060" y2="148" stroke={muted} stroke-width="3.5" marker-end="url(#rc-arrow)" />

        <rect x="30" y="154" width="640" height="102" fill={ink} fill-opacity="0.04" stroke={ink} stroke-width="2.5" />
        <text x="350" y="196" font-size="25" font-weight="600" fill={ink} text-anchor="middle">raw evidence</text>
        <text x="350" y="228" font-size="21" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">the declared reference policy</text>
        <rect x="770" y="154" width="640" height="102" fill={hpC} fill-opacity="0.08" stroke={hpC} stroke-width="2.5" />
        <text x="1090" y="196" font-size="25" font-weight="600" fill={hpC} text-anchor="middle">one compressed artifact per row</text>
        <text x="1090" y="228" font-size="21" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">content hash must match for every reader record</text>

        <line x1="350" y1="256" x2="640" y2="316" stroke={muted} stroke-width="3.5" marker-end="url(#rc-arrow)" />
        <line x1="1090" y1="256" x2="800" y2="316" stroke={muted} stroke-width="3.5" marker-end="url(#rc-arrow)" />
        <rect x="360" y="322" width="720" height="76" fill={paper} stroke={ink} stroke-width="2.5" />
        <text x="720" y="355" font-size="25" font-weight="600" fill={ink} text-anchor="middle">replay both policies across the panel</text>
        <text x="720" y="384" font-size="21" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">8 to 20 readers per panel, 11 model families</text>

        <line x1="540" y1="398" x2="380" y2="438" stroke={muted} stroke-width="3.5" marker-end="url(#rc-arrow)" />
        <line x1="900" y1="398" x2="1060" y2="438" stroke={muted} stroke-width="3.5" marker-end="url(#rc-arrow)" />
        <rect x="30" y="444" width="640" height="64" fill={hpC} fill-opacity="0.08" stroke={hpC} stroke-width="2.5" />
        <text x="350" y="484" font-size="24" font-weight="600" fill={hpC} text-anchor="middle">upgrade retention ρ = Δcomp / Δraw</text>
        <rect x="770" y="444" width="640" height="64" fill={mqC} fill-opacity="0.08" stroke={mqC} stroke-width="2.5" />
        <text x="1090" y="484" font-size="24" font-weight="600" fill={mqC} text-anchor="middle">excess ranking flips vs raw replay floor</text>
      </svg>
    </figure>
    <div class="method-note poster-body">
      <p>
        The endpoint pair is selected by <strong>raw score only</strong>, before compressed scores
        are inspected, and its compressed span reuses the same pair. Excess flips subtract the
        reversal rate of repeated raw-evidence evaluation on held-out rows, so ordering changes are
        counted <strong>beyond the panel's own row-sampling floor</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The primary study covers <strong>4 benchmarks and 5 compression families</strong> in a
        released 176,864-row interaction matrix. A method enters a panel only when every reader
        record has the same content hash for that row-level artifact. The analysis code performs
        this check; a shared method label alone does not admit the panel.
      </p>
    </div>
  </PosterCell>

  <PosterCell span={12} marker="3" kicker="Core result: prespecified confirmatory panels" title="Compression raises low-reader scores more and reduces the reader gap">
    <figure class="poster-figure">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 400" role="img" aria-label="Two scatter panels of reader score under raw versus compressed evidence. HotpotQA with fixed RECOMP retains 24.5% of a 31.8 point contrast across 20 readers; MuSiQue with a shared summary retains 0.8% of an 18.7 point contrast across 15 readers. Points sit far above the identity line at the low end.">
        {scalePanels.map((panel, p) => (
          <g>
            <text x={p * 740 + 380} y="24" text-anchor="middle" font-size="24" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="2" fill={panel.color}>{panel.title}</text>
            {scTicks.map((t) => (
              <>
                <line x1={scX(p, t)} y1="30" x2={scX(p, t)} y2="330" stroke={muted} stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 6" opacity="0.3" />
                <text x={scX(p, t)} y="360" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" fill={muted}>{t * 100}%</text>
                <line x1={scX(p, 0)} y1={scY(t)} x2={scX(p, 0.5)} y2={scY(t)} stroke={muted} stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 6" opacity="0.3" />
                <text x={scX(p, 0) - 14} y={scY(t) + 6} text-anchor="end" font-size="17" fill={muted}>{t * 100}%</text>
              </>
            ))}
            <line x1={scX(p, 0)} y1={scY(0)} x2={scX(p, 0.5)} y2={scY(0.5)} stroke={muted} stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="8 8" opacity="0.6" />
            <text x={scX(p, 0.335)} y={scY(0.3)} font-size="16" fill={muted}>identity</text>
            {panel.pts.map((pt, i) => (
              <g>
                <circle cx={scX(p, pt[0])} cy={scY(pt[1])} r="9" fill={panel.color} stroke={paper} stroke-width="2" />
                {(i === 0 || i === panel.pts.length - 1) && (
                  <circle cx={scX(p, pt[0])} cy={scY(pt[1])} r="16" fill="none" stroke={ink} stroke-width="2.5" />
                )}
              </g>
            ))}
            <text x={scX(p, 0.48)} y={scY(0.06)} text-anchor="end" font-size="22" font-weight="600" fill={panel.color}>{panel.note}</text>
            <text x={scX(p, 0.48)} y={scY(0.06) + 28} text-anchor="end" font-size="18" fill={muted}>{panel.readers}, same rows, same pools</text>
          </g>
        ))}
        <text x="34" y="180" font-size="18" fill={muted} transform="rotate(-90 34 180)" text-anchor="middle">compressed score</text>
        <text x="720" y="394" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" fill={muted}>raw score</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="poster-caption">
        Each point is one reader under raw and byte-identical compressed evidence; ringed points are
        the raw-selected endpoints. HotpotQA retention is 0.245 for EM and F1 (family-by-row
        intervals [-0.007, 0.379] and [0.050, 0.344]); the paired EIV correlation between raw score
        and compression gain is -.961 (EM). MuSiQue F1 retention is .008 [-.117, .270]; EM agrees in
        direction but is imprecise. The panel mean rises in both cases: this is floor-lifting with
        reader-dependent gains, not a common failure floor. Data: paper Figure 2 and Table 2.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </PosterCell>

  <PosterCell span={6} marker="4" kicker="Decision consequence: 5,000 row splits" title="Compression reverses reader orderings beyond row noise">
    <figure class="poster-figure">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 470" role="img" aria-label="Excess flip estimates with split-stability intervals: HotpotQA 16.7 points under EM and F1, MuSiQue 32.7 under EM and 21.2 under F1, all above the zero raw replay floor.">
        {flTicks.map((t) => (
          <>
            <line x1={flX(t)} y1="24" x2={flX(t)} y2="356" stroke={muted} stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 6" opacity={t === 0 ? 0 : 0.35} />
            <text x={flX(t)} y="396" text-anchor="middle" font-size="24" fill={muted}>{t > 0 ? `+${t}` : t}</text>
          </>
        ))}
        <line x1={flX(0)} y1="20" x2={flX(0)} y2="360" stroke={muted} stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="8 8" opacity="0.7" />
        <text x={flX(0)} y="440" text-anchor="middle" font-size="20" fill={muted}>raw replay floor</text>
        {flipRows.map((r, i) => {
          const y = 60 + i * 80;
          return (
            <g>
              <text x="26" y={y + 9} font-size="27" fill={ink}>{r.label}</text>
              <line x1={flX(r.lo)} y1={y} x2={flX(r.hi)} y2={y} stroke={r.color} stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round" />
              <circle cx={flX(r.c)} cy={y} r="13" fill={r.color} />
              <text x="1420" y={y + 9} text-anchor="end" font-size="28" font-weight="600" fill={r.color}>+{r.c.toFixed(1)}</text>
            </g>
          );
        })}
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="poster-caption">
        Median excess flip rates across 5,000 disjoint row splits, for reader pairs separated by at
        least 5pp; bars are 95% panel-conditional split-stability intervals. Raw replay flips only
        1.5% of eligible HotpotQA pairs, against roughly 18% under compression; the MuSiQue raw
        floor is zero. Data: paper Figure 3.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="winner-flip poster-body">
      <p class="winner-flip-head">One concrete decision change (MuSiQue F1, raw top-3 shortlist):</p>
      <p>
        <strong>DeepSeek R1 Distill Llama 70B</strong> wins under raw evidence.
        <span class="rc-mq">GPT-4.1-mini</span> wins under the shared summary.
      </p>
    </div>
  </PosterCell>

  <PosterCell span={6} marker="5" kicker="The account: row transitions" title="Rescue and damage coexist inside a rising average">
    <figure class="poster-figure">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 420" role="img" aria-label="Paired bars: HotpotQA RECOMP rescues 19.1% of row-reader pairs while damaging 35.7% of raw-correct pairs; MuSiQue rescues 22.9% and damages 33.8%.">
        {transRows.map((r, i) => {
          const y0 = 40 + i * 190;
          const wR = (r.rescue / 40) * 1080;
          const wD = (r.damage / 40) * 1080;
          return (
            <g>
              <text x="26" y={y0} font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill={r.color}>{r.label}</text>
              <rect x="290" y={y0 - 20} width={wR} height="46" fill={r.color} opacity="0.85" />
              <text x={290 + wR + 14} y={y0 + 12} font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill={r.color}>{r.rescue}%</text>
              <text x="290" y={y0 + 56} font-size="19" fill={muted}>rescued: raw-wrong, correct after compression (share of all row-reader pairs)</text>
              <rect x="290" y={y0 + 70} width={wD} height="46" fill={ink} opacity="0.55" />
              <text x={290 + wD + 14} y={y0 + 102} font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill={ink}>{r.damage}%</text>
              <text x="290" y={y0 + 146} font-size="19" fill={muted}>damaged: raw-correct pairs that become incorrect</text>
            </g>
          );
        })}
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="poster-caption">
        The two rates have different denominators and do not net into an accuracy change; they show
        substantial opposing movement inside the same average. Token F1 mass agrees: HotpotQA moves
        22.0% positive against 12.6% negative, MuSiQue 32.3% against 3.4%. Different readers reach
        similar compressed averages through different paths. Data: paper Table 3.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </PosterCell>

  <PosterCell span={6} marker="6" kicker="Validity check: four HotpotQA policies" title="Not every compressor collapses the curve">
    <figure class="poster-figure">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 400" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart of endpoint EM retention by HotpotQA policy: EXIT 0.836, RECOMP extractive 0.245, LLM summary 0.181, RECOMP abstractive 0.138.">
        {policyRows.map((r, i) => {
          const y = 30 + i * 92;
          const w = r.ret * 1000;
          return (
            <g>
              <text x="26" y={y + 14} font-size="25" fill={ink}>{r.label}</text>
              <rect x="330" y={y - 8} width="1000" height="44" fill={hpC} opacity="0.12" />
              <rect x="330" y={y - 8} width={w} height="44" fill={hpC} opacity={i === 0 ? 0.9 : 0.55} />
              <text x={330 + w + 14} y={y + 24} font-size="27" font-weight="600" fill={hpC}>.{Math.round(r.ret * 1000)}</text>
            </g>
          );
        })}
        <text x="330" y="392" font-size="20" fill={muted}>endpoint EM retention (1.0 = upgrade fully preserved)</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="poster-caption">
        Endpoint retention spans .098 to .836 across four HotpotQA evidence policies and two
        metrics; EXIT preserves most of the curve and its excess-flip intervals cross zero. The
        later 13-reader TriviaQA panel retains .428 (EM) and .391 (F1). The claim is that fixed
        compression <strong>can</strong> distort a comparison, not that every compressor does, so
        each deployed compressor needs its own audit. Data: paper §6.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </PosterCell>

  <PosterCell span={6} marker="7" kicker="Takeaway" title="Audit fidelity separately from utility" fill>
    <ol class="poster-body takeaway-list">
      <li><strong>Freeze the evidence.</strong> One retrieval pool and one compressed artifact per row, with recorded hashes; regenerated summaries are different evidence.</li>
      <li>Select weak, middle, and strong readers <strong>by raw score, before</strong> inspecting compressed scores.</li>
      <li>Replay both policies and report pipeline means, <span class="rc-hp">upgrade retention</span>, <span class="rc-mq">excess flips</span>, and rescue and damage.</li>
      <li>A rising average is not evidence of a preserved comparison: RECOMP helps several pipelines while hiding most of the HotpotQA upgrade.</li>
      <li>Raw evidence is the <strong>declared reference policy</strong>, not a claim about intrinsic model capability.</li>
    </ol>
  </PosterCell>

  <PosterCell span={12} marker="8" kicker="TL;DR">
    <div class="tldr-band poster-body">
      <div>
        <p class="tldr-head">What we did</p>
        <p>
          Fixed-Artifact Reader Replay: freeze rows, retrieval, and one
          <strong>byte-identical compressed artifact</strong> per row, then replay raw and
          compressed evidence across 8 to 20 readers. Four benchmarks, five compression families,
          and a released 176,864-row interaction matrix.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="tldr-head">What we found</p>
        <p>
          One useful in-domain RECOMP artifact cuts a <strong>31.8pp HotpotQA reader contrast to
          7.8pp</strong> (24.5% retention); MuSiQue F1 retains 0.8%. Both benchmarks reverse
          separated reader orderings beyond the raw replay floor, up to <strong>+32.7pp excess
          flips</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="tldr-head">What you should do</p>
        <p>
          Never compare readers behind an unaudited compression layer. Freeze the artifact, report
          raw and compressed scaling, and quantify retention and excess flips; a compressor that
          raises the average can still <strong>absorb the very upgrade you are measuring</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </PosterCell>
</PosterShell>

<style is:global>
  /* Paper palette (build_figures.py): HotpotQA/RECOMP blue #2F6F9F,
     MuSiQue/shared-summary amber #A65F00. */
  :root {
    --color-rc-hp: 47 111 159;
    --color-rc-mq: 166 95 0;
  }
</style>

<style>
  .rc-hp {
    color: rgb(var(--color-rc-hp));
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .rc-mq {
    color: rgb(var(--color-rc-mq));
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .span-collapse {
    margin-top: 6mm;
    border-top: 0.6mm solid rgb(var(--color-border-paper));
    padding-top: 5mm;
  }

  .big-stat {
    margin-top: 5mm;
    border-top: 0.6mm solid rgb(var(--color-border-paper));
    padding-top: 4mm;
    font-size: 20pt;
    line-height: 1.35;
